## Development Guidelines

### IPC Communication
- All IPC communication must go through the preload script
- Use `contextBridge.exposeInMainWorld()` for secure API exposure
- Never expose Node.js APIs directly to renderer

### Error Handling
- Use explicit error types and messages
- Log errors with sufficient context for debugging
- Never silently catch and ignore errors
- All errors must propagate to the UI layer with actionable messages

### Security
- Context isolation enabled
- Node integration disabled
- Sandbox mode enabled
- CSP headers configured

### TypeScript Standards
- Use strict mode
- Define proper types for all IPC channels
- Avoid `any` type unless absolutely necessary

### C++ Standards

**Mandatory Patterns** (for all C++ code in `packages/executor/`):
- **C++23 Standard** - Use latest language features (`std::expected`, `std::format`, concepts)
- **Zero-copy Data Flow** - pybind11 NumPy bindings, `std::span`, `std::move` semantics
- **Compile-time Optimization** - `consteval`, `constexpr`, static assertions, NTTP
- **Memory Sovereignty** - PMR pools, vector pre-allocation, cache-line alignment
- **Type Safety** - Strong types, `[[nodiscard]]`, `std::optional`, non-copyable RAII
- **Deterministic Execution** - `noexcept`, `std::chrono::steady_clock`, no exceptions on hot path

**Prohibited Patterns**:
- `new`/`delete` on hot paths (use PMR or object pools)
- `std::endl` (use `\n`)
- `virtual` functions in performance-critical code (use `std::variant` + `std::visit`)
- `std::shared_ptr` on hot paths (use raw pointers with clear ownership)
- Floating-point for prices (use fixed-point arithmetic)

### UI Standards
- **StratCraftsAI Design**: Deep Navy/Violet/Teal color palette, Glassmorphism, CyberGrid aesthetic
- **Theme Color System**: Use `--color-terminal-accent-primary` as single source of truth
- **Dropdown Portal**: Dropdown menus must use Portal + Floating UI to prevent overflow clipping

